  The great tip for fighting Master Kaen seems to be:  "Don't try
to use martial arts on him."  (Which has a parallel on the Wizard
Quest, where the Quest Leader warns you outright that the Quest
Nemesis is almost completely immune to harm by magical means.)

  Note that if you're *not* going to try using martial arts to 
kill Master Kaen, it doesn't matter if you're wearing body armor.


  The invocation items can be obtained in any order.  You can 
even locate the VS before going on the Quest.  So one option
is to do other things until you feel tough enough for Master 
Kaen.  (Who knows, maybe you'll get lucky and get your character
killed before you go on the Quest.  ;^)


  Do the Castle first and use the wand there to wish for a 
blessed figurine of an Archon.  (Heck, get two! ;-)  Then buff up
the Archon with with some +7 weapon and whatever +5 armor it will
wear.  (Then start selling tickets.  :-)


  (We just had a thread about this in the last couple of days.
Look for the subject "Master Kaen Hurts Me."  ;^)


  One approach would be sneaking up invisible and stealthy
and valiantly zapping Master Kaen with a wand of death before
he picks up the Eyes of the Overworld and gains magic resistance.
If you hit a trap and make noise, you're in trouble, so 's'earch
a lot before each move.  (Or zap wand/spell of secret door
detection/detect-unseen.)  

  Also, if some *other* monster on the level hits a trap and 
wakes MK, you're in trouble.  Be levitating, or wearing fireproof
water walking boots, and teleport over the lava.  (Presumably 
Master Kaen has not mastered walking on lava.  At least, not for
very long. :-)  While over the lava use some kind of ranged 
attack  ;^).  Remember, MK has MR, so use projectiles, wands of 
lightning/fire/cold(?), whatever.


  Since you can only fire one projectile at a time while 
levitating, you could try zapping a wand of cold straight
down while levitating over the lava to make an isolated square of
solid rock surrounded by lava.  Land on that to fire multiple 
projectiles per turn.  (Or use fireproof boots of water walking.
;-)

  The lava trick requires living long enough to get there, which 
is apparently difficult with an aware Master Kaen.  So either a) 
don't wake him up until your surrounded by lava or b) teleport to
over the lava.  (So let us know if the level is no teleport, 
would you? ;^)

  Comparing notes with Milton Pope (who started the "Master Kaen
Hurts Me" thread) might be a good idea.  He did some wizmode
testing, which left him dejected and sad.  (A nice funny YAAD
post might cheer Milton up.  ;^)

  A ring of free action and wielded potions of paralysis can do 
wonders in making vicious monsters sit quietly while you kill 
them.



